# Documentation Workflow

Loaded when user message starts with `doc:`. Human content lives under `docs/` only.

## Layout

```
docs/
├── README.md              # current milestone + links (keep ≤15 lines)
├── ROADMAP.md             # milestone checkboxes from path.txt
├── journal/               # session scratch
├── milestones/            # retrospective after acceptance test passes
└── learning/
    ├── ARCHITECTURE.md
    ├── DECISIONS.md
    └── GLOSSARY.md
```

## When to update what

| Target | When | Size |
|--------|------|------|
| `journal/` | Slice done, meaningful bug/insight, **end of session** | ~15 lines |
| `learning/GLOSSARY.md` | New term you'd explain twice | 1–3 lines/term |
| `learning/DECISIONS.md` | After choosing an approach | ~5 lines/ADR |
| `learning/ARCHITECTURE.md` | When fd/connection model changes (mainly M2+) | short |
| `milestones/` | **Only** after acceptance test in path.txt passes | full retrospective |
| `ROADMAP.md` | Checkbox when slice/milestone done | 1 line |

**Journal frequency:** 2–4 checkpoints per session + mandatory close. Not after every edit.

## Journal template

File: `docs/journal/YYYY-MM-DD-m<N>-s<N>.md`

```markdown
# M<N> Session <N> — YYYY-MM-DD

## Done
-

## Learned
-

## Open
-

## Next
-

## Commands
```

## `doc:` command map

| User says | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| `doc: end session` | Write/update today's journal using template |
| `doc: start session` | Read `ROADMAP.md` + latest journal; summarize status in 5 bullets |
| `doc: glossary <term>` | Append to `learning/GLOSSARY.md` |
| `doc: decision <title>` | Append ADR to `learning/DECISIONS.md` |
| `doc: milestone done` | Write `docs/milestones/m<N>-....md` only if acceptance test passed; update ROADMAP |
| `doc: architecture` | Update `learning/ARCHITECTURE.md` |

## Milestone retrospective (only after DoD passes)

Sections: Status, Definition of done, What we built, What we reused, What we learned, How to verify, Known limitations.

## Rules

- Bullets only in journal; no pasted AI essays.
- Never write milestone doc before acceptance test passes.
- Update `docs/README.md` link to latest journal when creating a new journal file.
